<title>USA: High Plains Wheat - Basis bids soften, trade slack.</title>
<headline>High Plains Wheat - Basis bids soften, trade slack.</headline>
<dateline>KANSAS CITY, Mo. 1997-03-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Basis bids for hard red winter wheat were steady to slightly softer Wednesday and movement remained slow, grain merchandisers said.</p>
<p>A Gulf exporter lowered its bid by three cents per bushel, and a grain merchandising firm in northeast Oklahoma lowered its bid by five cents overnight.</p>
<p>&quot;It's feeling weak -- it's pretty tough to sell anything,&quot; a dealer at the firm said, explaining why the firm dropped its bid.  </p>
